The punishment for the crime of gathering, providing information and documents aimed at using them against the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is death penalty. This is stated in the Criminal Code of Vietnam as follows: 

"1. Whoever commits one of the following acts shall be sentenced to life imprisonment or death:

a) Espionage, sabotage, or establishing a means for espionage, sabotage against the Socialist Republic of Vietnam;

b) Establishing a means for espionage, sabotage at the instruction of foreign countries; activities of surveillance, providing directions, harboring, leading, or any other action aiding foreigners in conducting espionage, sabotage;

c) Providing or collecting information and documents with the aim to provide state secrets to foreign countries; gathering, providing information and documents aimed at using them against the Socialist Republic of Vietnam."

Therefore, according to the Criminal Code of Vietnam, the punishment for the crime of gathering, providing information and documents with the aim to use them against the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is death penalty.
